WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.537
EXPLAIN shows PostgreSQL's planned execution strategy.

00:00:03.537 --> 00:00:08.547
This is useful for learning how the database intends to access and combine rows.

00:00:08.547 --> 00:00:13.842
In this tiny browser dataset, use the plan only to learn structure.

00:00:13.842 --> 00:00:21.147
Real performance tuning requires representative data volume, indexes, statistics, and workload.

00:00:21.147 --> 00:00:25.627
Do not make production performance claims from a small teaching example.

00:00:25.627 --> 00:00:29.502
SQL can express the same logic in several forms.

00:00:29.502 --> 00:00:35.722
A good rewrite keeps the same grain and business meaning while changing how work is organized.

00:00:35.722 --> 00:00:41.632
Use EXPLAIN to inspect the plan rather than assuming one style is always faster.

00:00:41.632 --> 00:00:45.583
Performance reasoning should follow correctness, not replace it.
